# Force LF line endings for text files regardless of local core.autocrlf.
# Without this, Windows' common core.autocrlf=true silently converts LF->CRLF
# on checkout, changing file bytes -- which breaks the SHA256 code-manifest
# checks inside frozen/*.json (e.g. test_frozen_definition_exists_after_freeze).
# This does not touch any source or frozen file content; it only makes future
# checkouts byte-identical to what is committed now.
* text=auto eol=lf
*.json -text
*.db binary
*.png binary
